      <span class="tg-hero__type">Part IV of Five</span>
      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">Testing Your Faith</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        Scripture does not tell believers to wonder. It gives them tests, states
        plainly that the tests are meant to produce knowledge, and expects most people
        who run them honestly to pass. This part sets out the tests, shows how they
        are meant to be run — and how they are commonly run in a way that produces the
        opposite of what they were given for — and then separates the two readers who
        need opposite words.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>I write these things to you who believe in the name of the Son of God, that
           you may know that you have eternal life.</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="1 John 5:13">1 John 5:13</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
